Modern Lakehouse Architecture with DataFusion, Parquet, and Plotly

Modern data platforms are increasingly moving toward lightweight lakehouse architectures that avoid expensive proprietary data warehouses and heavy distributed compute clusters. A powerful minimal stack can be built using Apache DataFusion, Apache Parquet, and Plotly. This stack allows organizations to build scalable analytics pipelines while significantly reducing infrastructure costs compared to traditional cloud data warehouses or managed compute clusters.

1. What Is a Modern Lakehouse?

A lakehouse combines the flexibility of a data lake with the structured analytics capabilities of a data warehouse.

Instead of storing data in expensive proprietary databases, data is stored in open formats on object storage and queried using scalable compute engines.

Typical architecture:

Raw Data Sources
       ↓
Data Lake Storage (Parquet files)
       ↓
Query Engine (DataFusion)
       ↓
Analytics / Visualization (Plotly dashboards)

This architecture enables:

SQL analytics

scalable storage

interactive data exploration

open data formats

2. Core Components of the Stack
Storage Layer — Parquet Data Lake

The foundation of the lakehouse is Apache Parquet, a highly efficient columnar format designed for analytical workloads.

Benefits:

Columnar compression

Efficient predicate pushdown

Reduced storage footprint

Compatible with many engines

Typical data lake layout:

data-lake/
   sales/
      part-001.parquet
      part-002.parquet
      part-003.parquet
   customers/
      part-001.parquet

Because Parquet is an open format, data can be accessed by many engines without vendor lock-in.

Query Engine — DataFusion

The compute layer is provided by Apache DataFusion, a high-performance SQL query engine built in Rust.

DataFusion capabilities include:

ANSI SQL support

vectorized execution

query optimization

predicate pushdown

Arrow-native processing

DataFusion operates directly on Parquet files without requiring a traditional database.

Example query:

SELECT country, SUM(sales)
FROM orders
GROUP BY country

Unlike heavy distributed engines, DataFusion can run embedded in applications, notebooks, or microservices.

Analytics Layer — Plotly

For visualization, the stack uses Plotly.

Plotly provides:

interactive dashboards

web-ready visualizations

notebook integration

real-time chart rendering

Example analytics flow:

SQL Query (DataFusion)
        ↓
Pandas DataFrame
        ↓
Interactive Visualization (Plotly)

This enables rapid exploratory analytics without needing a full BI platform.

3. End-to-End Architecture

A typical modern lightweight lakehouse looks like:

          Data Sources
      (APIs, logs, apps)
                ↓
        Data Lake Storage
          (Parquet files)
                ↓
      Query Engine Layer
         (DataFusion)
                ↓
         Data Processing
          (Python / SQL)
                ↓
     Interactive Analytics
            (Plotly)

This architecture is similar to enterprise lakehouse stacks used by:

Apache Spark

Trino

DuckDB

but implemented with much lighter infrastructure.

